arohalearning.com,0,"Aroha Consulting &amp; Training Aroha Consulting & Training Skip to content HOME About Guest Speaker Services by Sector Welcome to Aroha Consulting and Training At Aroha Consulting and Training, we believe education should be engaging, empowering, and deeply human. Led by educator and trainer Adalia Ellis, Aroha Consulting and Training provides learner-centered training, workshops, and consulting services that build confidence, communication skills, and meaningful connection across diverse communities. What We Do With over 20 years of experience in education, public speaking, and community-based programming, Aroha Consulting and Training specializes in interactive workshops, professional development, and curriculum design that meet people where they are. Our offerings blend practical skill-building with creativity, cultural awareness, and social-emotional learning—supporting individuals, organizations, and youth in developing the tools they need to communicate effectively, collaborate with others, and thrive personally and professionally. Whether you’re seeking engaging professional training, educational workshops, or transformative learning experiences rooted in equity, wellness, and real-world application, Aroha Consulting and Training is here to support growth—with intention, care, and purpose. Serving Communities, Institutions & Individuals Click your sector to discover customized learning and training options. Corporate University Public School Individuals & Communities About Adalia With over two decades of educational experience, Adalia is a seasoned educator, having passionately engaged in and crafted educational programs at both grassroots and formal classroom levels. Her journey as a public speaker commenced at the tender age of 10, and she further honed her oratory skills during her four-year tenure as a Toastmasters member in her twenties. She went on to teach public speaking as a faculty member at Francis Marion University from 2018-2025. Beyond the realm of public speaking, Adalia’s heart is drawn to the transformative power of dance, which she views as a conduit for rejuvenation, storytelling, healing, and community building. With 18 years of experience as a dance instructor, both overseas and in the United States, she has witnessed the profound wellness that dance can impart. Adalia is an alumna of Coastal Carolina University, holding a Bachelor of Arts Degree in History and Theater, as well as a Masters Degree in Teaching. These qualifications have equipped her with the expertise to craft engaging and transformational curriculum, furthering her mission of fostering unity and understanding through a variety of programs and modalities. Outside of her professional pursuits, Adalia is a loving wife and devoted mother who enjoys camping, reading, watching movies, exploring the world through travel, and engaging in meaningful conversations. Her multifaceted life experiences and unwavering commitment to justice and unity define her as a compassionate leader and educator. Adalia was truly a godsend when I needed coaching to prepare for an important presentation. From the very beginning, she understood that I needed more than just traditional coaching. I also had to work through my anxiety and nervousness. With patience and care, she guided me through breathing techniques and calming exercises, then had me write affirmations to help build my confidence. Afterward, I did a practice run of my presentation with her, and her thoughtful feedback gave me the tools I needed to deliver it with clarity and ease. The result? Just one week after my presentation, I received my dream job offer! I am beyond grateful for Adalia’s support, encouragement, and expertise. She made all the difference. Tamara Curriculum Vitae Adalia Ellis Email: arohalearningsc@gmail.com PROFESSIONAL PROFILE Educator and public speaking professional with over 20 years of experience teaching communication skills to diverse audiences, including university students, educators, and adult lear"
