dodgeflock.org,0,"DodgeFlock — Dodge County citizens against networked ALPRs A citizens’ movement in Dodge County, Wisconsin. Ask your County Board supervisor to ban networked ALPR / Flock cameras and multi-agency location sharing. Privacy isn’t partisan. DodgeFlock — Dodge County citizens against networked ALPRs Skip to content Surveillance camera DodgeFlock Get the flock out of Dodge. Menu Home The problem In the news Camera map About Contact your supervisor Dodge County, Wisconsin · Nonpartisan privacy campaign Ask your supervisor to ban networked plate readers in Dodge County. Dodge County already has Flock-style ALPR cameras logging where vehicles drive. Those records can be searched and shared across agencies—often without a warrant. Tell the County Board: no county purchase, lease, or operation of networked ALPRs—and no multi-agency sharing of that location data. Privacy isn’t partisan. Get the flock out of Dodge. Contact your supervisor Camera map Key facts (public sources) 18 Dodge County SO Flock ALPRs Atlas of Surveillance, as of Sep 2025 42 Community-mapped cameras DeFlock/OSM filter · Dodge County (floor) ~20 WisDOT ROW mounts · Dodge Co SO Deflock Dane WisDOT ALPR map (+ Horicon 4, Beaver Dam 1, Lomira 1) 0 Public county Flock contract / Board approval found File a Wisconsin Open Records request with County Clerk / Sheriff / Purchasing for contracts, invoices, sharing agreements, and Board packets. The ask: Tell the County Board: no county purchase, lease, or operation of networked ALPRs—and no multi-agency sharing of that location data. Privacy is not a left/right issue Both civil-liberties groups and conservative constitutional litigators are raising the same concern: warrantless mass location tracking . ACLU of Wisconsin / EFF ACLU-WI says Flock remains “incredibly invasive” mass surveillance whose use “should require a warrant based on probable cause,” plus independent oversight— not police self-policing. EFF argues networked ALPRs are purpose-built to track everyone regardless of suspicion. WILL (conservative / liberty) The Wisconsin Institute for Law & Liberty sued Waukesha County and 11 municipalities (Sep 10, 2026), arguing warrantless Flock Location Database searches violate the Fourth Amendment and seeking a warrant requirement before searches. What you can do 1. Contact your supervisor Districts 1–33. Pick yours, use the talking points, send from our form. Contact your supervisor 2. See where cameras are mapped Dodge plus adjoining counties—community-mapped network footprint (incomplete floor). Camera map 3. Follow what’s in the news Chetek, Oconomowoc, Racine, Milwaukee, WILL lawsuit, and more. In the news DodgeFlock Get the flock out of Dodge. · Privacy isn’t partisan. Ban networked ALPRs in Dodge County · Not affiliated with county government DodgeFlock is an independent advocacy site — not a county office or department. Camera locations are community-mapped (DeFlock/OSM, ODbL) and may be incomplete. See maps.deflock.org . Contacts from public county rosters — verify before outreach. Privacy Policy · Terms of Use"
