garyforourneighborhoods.com,0,"Gary McCoy for Supervisor! Gary McCoy for Supervisor! 0 Skip to Content About Priorities Endorsements Open Menu Close Menu About Priorities Endorsements Open Menu Close Menu About Priorities Endorsements Gary McCoy Gary McCoy has deep roots in both local and national government. He’s running for Supervisor to put his experience to use for our district. San Francisco can deliver safer streets, thriving businesses, and more housing. Gary knows how. About Gary Gary grew up in Norfolk, Virginia. He moved to San Francisco in 2002, where he overcame addiction, homelessness, and an HIV diagnosis. Gary has been sober for over 15 years. Gary lives with his husband, Kory, and their dog, Xander, in the Castro. Gary has served as Nancy Pelosi’s political director, as aide to then-Supervisor Scott Wiener, and as leader of San Francisco’s two LGBTQ Democratic Clubs. “He’s trusted, tested, and ready to deliver for our City and District. When Gary speaks, I listen.” — Endorsed By Speaker Emerita Nancy Pelosi Priorities Expand Housing & Transit Gary will take on the housing crisis by cutting red tape so we can build new housing of all kinds faster, while also strengthening tenant protections. He will support funding that improves our transit reliability and extends service hours. Thriving Small Businesses Gary will address storefront vacancies by streamlining the city’s permitting process and continuing the “First Year Free” program for new businesses. He’ll also grow programs that support our longstanding anchor and legacy businesses."
