lakshay.fyi,0,"Lakshay Agarwal, Software engineer Lakshay Agarwal builds products end to end: checkout and payments, security and compliance review, and the whole user journey. Currently building the booking platform for PVR Cinemas. Lakshay Agarwal, Software engineer Skip to content LA Lakshay Agarwal Home Work About Writing Email me 0 1 Home 0 2 Work 0 3 About 0 4 Writing lakshayagarwal50@gmail.com Replies within a day Software that takes payments, passes the audit, and ships. I design and build products end to end, then stay accountable for them in production. Right now: the booking platform for PVR Cinemas. See how it works Email me Companies bring me in for the parts of a product where a mistake costs money: checkout and payments , security and compliance review , and the whole journey from first click to confirmation. I have shipped through VAPT and PCI DSS reviews, so the audit is part of the plan, not a surprise at the end. The engineering version Stack Next.js App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Redux Toolkit, Tailwind. Node and Python where needed. Payments Razorpay full lifecycle: order, auth, webhook verification, reconciliation, compensating refunds, wallets. Browser WASM codecs and Web Workers for heavy work. Virtualized tables, normalized state, memoized selectors. Review CSP, token handling, dependency audits, PCI scope on the frontend. Findings closed before launch. Based in Noida / Delhi NCR Working as Software engineer Open to Full-time and freelance Replies Within a day Four systems, one workbench Each drawing reads on its own. Press Run to watch it happen, or turn on engineering detail to see what runs underneath every step. Engineering detail Systems PVR ticket checkout from picking a seat to a ticket on the phone SnapWap from a dropped photo to a smaller file HR portal five modules, one source of truth Pipeline inspection from sensor noise to a short review list 4 of 4 loaded PVR ticket checkout from picking a seat to a ticket on the phone Next.js, Redux Toolkit, Razorpay Customer picks seats Seat selection seat slice, 480s hold timer Pays Payment Razorpay order + authorization Seat is locked in Booking confirmed webhook verify, reconcile, write Booking step fails Refund goes out automatically. Nobody is charged for a seat they did not get. compensating refund, seat released, idempotent retry reverse payment Ticket on their phone QR ticket issued QR issuance, share link Customer picks seats Pays Seat is locked in Ticket on their phone Seat selection Payment Booking confirmed QR ticket issued Booking step fails Refund goes out automatically. Nobody is charged for a seat they did not get. compensating refund, seat released, idempotent retry reverse payment seat slice, 480s hold timer Razorpay order + authorization webhook verify, reconcile, write QR issuance, share link Run Run with a failure Drop a photo Read the image createImageBitmap, main thread Pick a format and size Resize and reduce Lanczos3, libimagequant (WASM) Compare side by side Make two versions MozJPEG / WebP / AVIF / JXL / OxiPNG All of this happens on your computer. Nothing is uploaded. Web Workers; sequence IDs + AbortController cancel stale jobs when a slider moves Download File on your device Blob URL, batch ZIP Drop a photo Pick a format and size Compare side by side Download Read the image Resize and reduce Make two versions File on your device All of this happens on your computer. Nothing is uploaded. Web Workers; sequence IDs + AbortController cancel stale jobs when a slider moves createImageBitmap, main thread Lanczos3, libimagequant (WASM) MozJPEG / WebP / AVIF / JXL / OxiPNG Blob URL, batch ZIP Run Five HR modules that work on their own and still agree with each other Attendance slice + entityAdapter Leave slice + approvals Payroll slice + virtual table Onboarding slice + RBAC guards Reports selectors + CSV Approve a leave once, and attendance, payroll and reports all update shared middleware: leave.approved -> attendance.recalc, payroll.adjust; memoized selectors keep 500+ rows instant Five HR modules that work on their own and still agree with each other Attendance Leave Payroll Onboarding Reports Approve a leave once, and attendance, payroll and reports all"
